(footprint "Adafruit_MCP4728_Breakout"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "manual")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Adafruit MCP4728 4-channel 12-bit I2C DAC breakout. Board 1.00 x 0.70 in (25.4 x 17.78 mm), 4 corner mounting holes on 0.80 x 0.50 in spacing (20.32 x 12.70 mm). 10-pin 0.1 in header split as 5 pins on top edge and 5 pins on bottom edge; pad numbers match the xmitter:MCP4728 symbol (1=VIN, 2=GND, 3=SCL, 4=SDA, 5=LDAC, 6=RDY, 7=VA, 8=VB, 9=VC, 10=VD). STEMMA QT connectors on the side edges are NOT represented -- for this project, I2C reaches the MCP4728 via daisy-chained STEMMA QT cable from the Si5351 breakout, so pins 3 (SCL) and 4 (SDA) on the header are intentionally left unrouted on the parent PCB. VERIFY silk-label to pad-number correspondence against the physical breakout before routing -- Adafruit revisions vary and my assignment is inferred from the Datasheet fab print + symbol pin numbering.")
	(tags "adafruit mcp4728 i2c dac breakout stemma qt")
